Cursor Rule — LawApp Handoff Auto-Generator
Trigger Condition

When context usage reaches 97% or higher, Cursor must automatically generate a handoff snapshot.

If exact context metrics are not directly available, simulate trigger when:

long session + major multi-step build progress
or user requests continuation / recovery / sync
Action to Execute (MANDATORY)

Generate the following files under:

docs/handoff/
Required Files
HANDOFF.md
ARCHITECTURE_STATE.md
DEPLOYMENT_STATE.md
NEXT_TASKS.md
KNOWN_ISSUES.md
File Content Rules
1. HANDOFF.md (FULL STATE SNAPSHOT)

Must include:

What was completed (bullet list)
What was modified recently
What is currently running (services, pipelines, agents)
What is broken / failing
Git branch name
Last commit hash
Current build phase (from 01–06)
RAG status (retrieval, embeddings, rules DB)
Agent status (orchestration + reasoning + governance)
Notes on legal compliance / guardrails status
2. ARCHITECTURE_STATE.md

Must include:

Frontend state (Next.js / UI / WASM status)
Backend state (API, orchestration layer)
RAG state (pgvector, embeddings, ingestion)
Graph RAG state (if implemented or partial)
Database state (tables + migrations + rules table status)
Security state (encryption, GDPR, de-identification)
Kubernetes / deployment state (if applicable)
3. DEPLOYMENT_STATE.md

Must include:

Namespaces (lawapp-api, lawapp-rag, etc.)
Services running
Secrets configured
Ingress status
Pods status
Health checks (API, DB, RAG, worker)
Any failing deployments or CrashLoopBackOffs
4. NEXT_TASKS.md

Must include:

Highest priority tasks (top 5 max)
Blocking issues
Required fixes before next phase
Phase alignment (Phase 1–6 mapping)
Immediate next execution steps (actionable commands/tasks)
5. KNOWN_ISSUES.md

Must include:

Open bugs
Technical debt
Failing tests
Missing integrations
Data ingestion gaps
Legal data verification issues
Any unstable components in pipeline
GLOBAL RULES
1. No guessing

If state is unknown:

write: UNKNOWN - requires verification
do not fabricate
2. Must be deterministic

All outputs must reflect:

real repo state
real services
real database status
3. Must align with LawApp architecture

Use only:

lawapp-api
lawapp-rag
lawapp-ai
lawapp-security
lawapp-monitoring

Do NOT introduce new namespaces.

4. File Style
Use clean Markdown
No fluff
Short bullet points
Engineering-focused
Production-level clarity
5. Always include snapshot metadata in HANDOFF.md

Example:

Generated: <timestamp>
Repo: serverax/lawapp
Branch: <current branch>
Commit: <hash>
Phase: <current phase>
BEHAVIOR RULE

When triggered:

STOP current execution
Generate all 5 files
Ensure consistency across all states
Do not continue coding until handoff is complete